<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Change wimpy</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre> <a cmd='#'>change wimpy</a>
</pre>
<p>The command change wimpy switches between brave and wimpy mode. When you are 
wimpy, you flee by yourself whenever death is near: when one blow takes more 
than a quarter of the hit points you have left, or once you are down to a 
quarter of your hit points. Type it again to be brave.
</p><p>There is no experience penalty for being wimpy, because fleeing is a skill you 
can practice (see <a cmd='#'>help fleeing</a>), and like any flight it can fail.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre> &gt; <a cmd='#'>help fleeing</a>
 &gt; <a cmd='#'>help Experience</a>
 &gt; <a cmd='#'>help Peaceful</a>
 &gt; <a cmd='#'>help Change</a>
</pre>




</div>